model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      constraint "The pool image publication receipt is not memoized, so each sequential release phase rewrites it inside the runner's private mkdtemp directory. Post-deploy image verification computes this candidate's pool image input from its own source with the deploy's function. Without a bound fleet it proves the root application against the published digest as before. Once the PoolWorker binds a blue/green fleet the release pins the root to its baseline image, so a release skips the root and proves the fleet: POOL_DESIRED_IMAGE_INPUT must equal the candidate's computed input, and each bound application once against its own immutable configured digest, and at least one running instance in an application whose image input equals POOL_DESIRED_IMAGE_INPUT; starting or stopping fleet cells are skipped, not refused. Each missing, malformed, foreign, duplicate or stale fact refuses with the exact binding or field. Recorded recovery reads no Worker bindings and never substitutes a fleet for its exact old container. The read-only Check probe has no candidate input; it proves the current baseline, keeping the root path while the root serves, and runs the same verifier against the native production baseline whenever the verifier or its probe changes. Both release deploy jobs (main and manual) allow 180 minutes so that a healthy multi-phase release is never cancelled between an upload and its activation."
    }
  }
}
